Hello everyone,

Just a few questions.

How the number of sightings influences the final result, for example: I was asked to analyze white-tailed deer data, but they only have 36 sightings for an area of ​​10k Ha.
The initial results tell me that the density is 0.089, and a population of 892 individuals (Hazard-Rate / Hermite), with CDS analysis.

Do I need a minimum number of sightings? What does a coefficient of variation of 45.7% mean?

I know that my questions may seem basic to many of you, but I've been a couple of years in this, I'm from Peru and there are not many people who work with that, so I want to develop more in this area. Thank you very much for all the contributions.

